Historical maps
===============

Each map below is downloaded only when a person adds it in Map Vietnam. The full list, with each
map's download addresses, is data/sources/map_library.json.

US Army Map Service series L7014, with border sheets L7015 and L7016, 1:50,000 (mostly
1965-1970), 498 sheets
  Downloaded from the USGS Store (store.usgs.gov), GeoPDFs prepared by the US National
  Geospatial-Intelligence Agency. Works of the US Government: public domain in the United States.
  The PDF metadata carries release code "DS" or "OO"; check the printed margin of a sheet before
  redistributing tiles made from it.

Joint Operations Graphic (Air), series 1501A, 1:250,000 (about 1966-2000), 34 sheets
  US Defense Mapping Agency; GeoPDFs prepared by the US National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency,
  downloaded from the USGS Store, or, when the Store fails (and for NC 48-5 and NF 48-10, which
  the Store lacks), from the Perry-Castaneda Library Map
  Collection, University of Texas Libraries (https://maps.lib.utexas.edu/maps/jog/vietnam/).
  Works of the US Government: public domain in the United States. Some PDFs carry release code
  "DS"; check the printed margin before redistributing tiles. When a file came from the
  University of Texas, credit: "Courtesy of the University of Texas Libraries, The University of
  Texas at Austin".

US Army Map Service series L909, city plans, 1:12,500 (1963-1971), 18 towns
  GeoPDFs prepared by the US National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency, downloaded from the USGS
  Store. Works of the US Government: public domain in the United States. Release code "ZZ/DS";
  check the printed margin of a plan before redistributing tiles made from it.

Carte de l'Indochine 1:100,000 (Service Geographique de l'Indochine, 1895-1952), 298 sheets
  Fonds de cartes de l'Indochine francaise du Centre IST REGARDS (CNRS), published on NAKALA
  (collection https://nakala.fr/collection/10.34847/nkl.16bcmpc6), downloaded through NAKALA's
  IIIF image service. Each sheet has its own licence, recorded with it in
  data/sources/map_library.json and shown in the viewer: most are CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/: non-commercial use only, with attribution,
  adaptations shared alike), some CC BY 4.0. Credit: "Centre IST REGARDS (CNRS), NAKALA" and the
  sheet's record. The control points in data/scans/sgi100k_*.json were computed for this project
  from each sheet's printed graticule (Apache-2.0).

US Army Map Service series L509, Indochina and Thailand, 1:250,000 (1950s-1960s), 32 sheets
  Scans by the Perry-Castaneda Library Map Collection, University of Texas Libraries
  (https://maps.lib.utexas.edu/maps/ams/indochina_and_thailand/). Works of the US Government;
  the library describes such maps as public domain. Credit: "Courtesy of the University of Texas
  Libraries, The University of Texas at Austin".

British Admiralty charts (UK Hydrographic Office, 1855-1964), 8 charts
  Scans on Wikimedia Commons (https://commons.wikimedia.org), marked public domain (Crown
