Records
=======

NGA GEOnet Names Server (GNS), Vietnam country file
  US National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency, fetched from an Internet Archive capture of
  geonames.nga.mil. US Government work. NGA asks for this credit: "Toponymic information is based
  on the Geographic Names Database, containing official standard names approved by the United
  States Board on Geographic Names and maintained by the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency."

Hamlet Evaluation System gazetteers (RG 472) and Combat Area Casualties Current File (RG 330)
  US National Archives and Records Administration (catalog.archives.gov). US federal records,
  public domain, access and use unrestricted.

THOR, Theater History of Operations, Vietnam air operations
  US Air Force data, published on Kaggle as usaf/vietnam-war-bombing-operations. US Government
  work, public domain; the Kaggle dataset is marked CC0. Kaggle serves it without an account at the
  time of writing; if it asks for a key, a free account supplies one.

Wikipedia
  English Wikipedia "List of United States servicemembers and civilians missing in action during
  the Vietnam War" and Vietnamese Wikipedia "Danh sach Di tich quoc gia Viet Nam" and "Di tich
  quoc gia dac biet (Viet Nam)", with article coordinates. Text and data by Wikipedia
  contributors, licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). Every
  record keeps a link to its page.

Wikidata
  Data from Wikidata (https://www.wikidata.org), dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0.

OpenStreetMap
  Data (C) OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open Database License 1.0
  (https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/). See https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright.

Vietnam Helicopter Pilots Association (VHPA), optional
  Copyright VHPA. Only short factual fields are stored (dates, tail numbers, grids, status codes,
  places); no narrative text is stored or quoted. It is downloaded only if the user chooses it.


